# Cloudflare Pages headers for the static app.
#
# The app is a static shell that talks to the Worker API. The API's own
# security headers are set in Rust on every `/v1/*` response (Cratefield
# harness, architecture section 6, issue #435) and on the email-verify page
# (`crates/livingbrain-workspaces/src/handlers.rs`, `verify_page`); these
# mirror them here so the *static* pages carry the same guarantees before a
# request ever reaches the Worker.
#
# `_headers` has no block-comment syntax: `#` is the only comment marker. Every
# other line is either a route path or an indented `Name: value` rule — so the
# `/*` below is the wildcard route covering every page, not an opening
# delimiter, and nothing else here may be wrapped in `/* */`.
#
# The inline theme bootstrap in each page's <head> is the one inline script —
# it is genuinely needed there, because it has to run before the first paint or
# the page flashes the wrong theme, and a deferred module runs after it. Its
# SHA-256 is in the CSP below and is identical across all three pages, because
# the script is byte-identical. If you edit it, recompute the hash with the
# raw text between the tags — the browser hashes the exact text content of the
# element, so the leading newline and the trailing indentation before
# </script> must be kept (do NOT strip it):
#   python3 -c "import re,hashlib,base64; s=open('app/index.html').read(); print(base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(re.search(r'<script>(.*?)</script>', s, re.S).group(1).encode()).digest()).decode())"
# and update it below. Nothing else may be inlined: `script-src` has no
# 'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval', so anything new must move to a file
# under assets/ and be loaded with <script type="module">.

# Every route: the CSP and the security headers.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-GsRRMiFErXfPA/V4np3z0CtFFGhxjhelBLl+TjY8sYA='; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self' https://github.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Caching (tools/stamp-assets.mjs builds what is deployed; app/ is its source).
#
# The pages are revalidated on every load, so a deploy is visible on the next
# one. `private`: the session is an HttpOnly cookie on the API and no page
# carries per-person data, but a shared cache still never keeps a copy. Each
# page is listed under both spellings, because the assets server answers
# `/wiki.html` with a redirect to `/wiki` and the rule matches the request path.
/
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/settings
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/settings.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/wiki
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/wiki.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/brain
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache
/brain.html
  Cache-Control: private, no-cache

# Content-hashed copies: the name changes whenever the bytes do, so a copy is
# good forever. Every page, module import, stylesheet url(), manifest icon and
# the service worker's precache list points here.
/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The unhashed originals, at the paths the Worker's device pages link by name
# (`/assets/app.css`, `/assets/device.css`, `/assets/favicon.svg`) and an
# already-open pre-deploy page may still ask for. Revalidated every time, so
# they can never be an hour behind. Not under `/static/`, so the two rules
# never both apply to one file.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache
# The worker and the manifest are rebuilt with every deploy, at fixed names.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache
